  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f2f9ec81392f3254b96fef70765aaae9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Debrief_COC2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CircuitCrafter.Assessment.ModuleDebriefData
  moduleId: COC2
  headline: Cable made, addresses set, and the two machines can see each other. What
    counts now is whether you could do it again on someone else's network.
  practiceNotice: 
  assessorNotes:
  - outcomeCode: "LO1 \xB7 Install network cables"
    assessorLooksFor: "An assessor checks your pinout against the standard you named
      \u2014 T568A or T568B, the same at both ends unless you meant a crossover \u2014
      and looks for the jacket seated inside the connector, not just for the click."
  - outcomeCode: "LO2 \xB7 Set network configuration"
    assessorLooksFor: You are judged on whether the address is consistent with the
      mask and gateway you were given, and on whether you can say why an address
      is usable rather than reciting one from a worksheet.
  - outcomeCode: "LO3 \xB7 Set router/Wi-Fi/wireless access point/repeater configuration"
    assessorLooksFor: The assessor looks for default credentials changed, an SSID
      and security mode chosen deliberately, and settings you can explain. A working
      link on an open network is not a pass.
  - outcomeCode: "LO4 \xB7 Inspect and test the configured computer networks"
    assessorLooksFor: Testing means proving it in both directions and reading the
      actual output. "Request timed out" with a reason you can name beats a ping
      you ran and did not look at.
  nextButtonLabel: Take the assessment
  nextSceneName: 
  nextButtonLabelAfterAssessment: 
  nextSceneNameAfterAssessment: 
  replayButtonLabel: Run it again
